{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-tm-worked-examples-table1-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:tm-worked-examples-table1-data","kind":"table","title":"Table 1 from tm-worked-examples","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tm-worked-examples"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"tm-worked-examples-table1-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"tbl:tm-worked-examples-table1-data\"></a><p>The two crossings at generator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0</code> of the Helium-3 nucleon strand <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[\\mathfrak{p}_0, \\mathfrak{p}_1, \\mathfrak{n}_2]</code>. Each row lists the crossing (its pair of strand positions), the nucleon pair it joins, the crossing type — proton-proton (pp) or proton-neutron mixed (mix) — and the transfer matrix that type contributes: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{pp}</code> for a like-nucleon crossing, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{\\mathrm{mix}}</code> for a proton-neutron crossing.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Crossing</th>\n<th>Pair</th>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Transfer matrix</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(0, 1)</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{p}_0</code>-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{p}_1</code></td>\n<td>pp</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{pp}</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(0, 2)</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{p}_0</code>-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{n}_2</code></td>\n<td>mix</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{\\mathrm{mix}}</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-mass-binding-algorithms/tm-worked-examples-table1-data.md","heading":"Table","page":"b/tbl-tm-worked-examples-table1-data","qa":{"counts":{"pass":41,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":0}}}
